### PREDICTIONS -- DECLARED BEFORE THIS RUN (G11's requirement) ###

P18.1 is ADDITIVE. It adds two production translation units
(src/species/SpeciesRegistry.cpp, src/species/MassFractionState.cpp) and one test file
(tests/unit/species/test_mass_fraction_state.cpp). NO existing source file is modified
except the two CMakeLists.txt lines that compile them. Every pre-existing count must
therefore be UNCHANGED, and the only movement must be the new tests.

gtest_discover_tests registers ONE CTEST ROW PER GTEST TEST, so the 60 new gtest tests
(12 SpeciesRegistryTest + 48 MassFractionStateTest, counted from --gtest_list_tests at
results/p18/multi_species_state/logs/07_test_counts.log) add 60 rows to every
configuration. None of them matches the 5 frozen exclusion patterns, so selected rises
by 60 too. Skipped and DISABLED must NOT move: the new tests are neither.

  BASELINE (P18.0)                      PREDICTED (P18.1 = baseline + 60)
  release_cuda 2763 sel 2712 P 0 F  ->  2823 selected, 2772 Passed, 0 FAILED, 2 Skipped, 49 DISABLED
  cpu_only     2540 sel 2493 P 0 F  ->  2600 selected, 2553 Passed, 0 FAILED, 0 Skipped, 47 DISABLED
  debug_gui    2825 sel 2770 P 4 F  ->  2885 selected, 2830 Passed, 4 FAILED, 2 Skipped, 49 DISABLED

  THE 4 DEBUG+GUI FAILURES ARE EXPECTED AND INHERITED, not a P18.1 regression:
    DriverSeegmiller.MeshSequence, .CorrectedSequenceIsDeterministic,
    DriverSeegmillerInlet.MappedInletPreservesTheMassFlow, .MediumGridAB
  all four TIMEOUT at the frozen 7200 s. They pass in both Release configurations and are
  pre-P17 tests; Debug is >3.8x-6.0x slower than the limit was set for. P17.11 left G10 at
  PARTIAL for exactly this. The timeout is NOT raised here either.
  results/p17/qualification/G10_DEBUG_GUI_TIMEOUTS.md

  ANY DEVIATION FROM THESE NUMBERS IS A P18.1 FINDING. A FIFTH failure, a changed
  Skipped/DISABLED count, or a delta other than exactly +60 all mean P18.1 was not additive.

